# Line endings: LF everywhere, in the repository AND in the working tree.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS: without it, `core.autocrlf=true` (the Git for Windows
# default) checks files out with CRLF while the index stores LF. Prettier
# defaults to `endOfLine: "lf"`, so eslint-plugin-prettier then reports a
# `Delete ␍` error on every single line of every CRLF file — `bun lint` failed
# with ~4,600 errors on a clean Windows checkout while CI stayed green, because
# GitHub Actions runs ubuntu-latest and checks out LF.
#
# `eol=lf` overrides core.autocrlf, so every contributor on every platform gets
# exactly the line endings CI lints against. Git still normalizes on commit, so
# this changes no committed content — only what lands on disk.
#
# After changing this file, refresh existing working copies with:
#   git add --renormalize .
#   git rm --cached -r . && git reset --hard
* text=auto eol=lf

# vCard is the one format that genuinely requires CRLF: RFC 6350 §3.2 defines
# the line break as CRLF, and this file is served straight to contact apps from
# public/. It was already being deployed with LF (CI builds on ubuntu, so the
# checkout was LF regardless of what Windows had locally) — pinning it here fixes
# that for the deployed artifact too, not just the working copy.
*.vcf text eol=crlf

# Binaries — never normalize, never diff as text.
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.webp  binary
*.ico   binary
*.pdf   binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf   binary
*.otf   binary

# Generated: keep it out of diffs and review noise. TanStack regenerates it on
# every build; it is committed only so typecheck works on a fresh clone.
src/routeTree.gen.ts linguist-generated=true
